Suggested upstream change for subscript 10.8.1 (from jz's src/parse.js, which
carries the same rules as layers over subscript's parse.id and parse.space).

- feature/unicode.js: a name is ID_Start, then ID_Continue, `$`, `_`, ZWNJ or
  ZWJ, raw, as a surrogate pair or escaped; an escape must spell a name
  character. The id test took every code unit from U+00C0 but × and ÷: it
  missed ª µ º (ID_Start) and · (ID_Continue) and took whitespace, line
  terminators, symbols and punctuation for letters. The private use area stays
  a name's, for the template tag's placeholders. The space layer skips NBSP,
  ZWNBSP, LS, PS and the space separators.
- feature/unicode-id.js, util/gen-unicode-id.js: the range tables, generated
  from Node's Unicode data. Tables, not \p{…}: jz compiles subscript into its
  own compiler, whose regular expressions carry no Unicode property tables.
- feature/asi.js, feature/comment.js: CR, LS and PS end a line as LF does, for
  ASI (`break` LS `L` is two statements) and for a `//` comment.
- test/unicode.js: `\u{1F600}` (an emoji) is no name; the scaling test used
  unassigned code points after U+086A.

